  "asr_text": "The people behind the prize say it is an effort to ask other literary prizes, which are struggling with how to handle writers' use of AI, a question. They create one prize and ask the others, so what would you do? You might call it a question in the shape of a trophy. For example, what if you were reading a story late into the night, and just after the last line moved you, you heard, actually, I wrote it with AI? Would a line that had seemed beautiful suddenly feel distant, or would you say, I enjoyed it, so I have no complaint? A special judging meeting might begin inside the reader's mind. Of course, the label, co-written with AI alone, doesn't guarantee an interesting story. I wouldn't decide I wanted to read it based on that alone either. What I want to know is what kind of story it is and what the writing is like. Before the label, I want to see the first page.",
